      "hints": [
        "Rearrange $y = -3(x-2)^2 + 14$ to make $(x-2)^2$ the subject.",
        "Take the negative square root since $x \\le 2$.",
        "Solve for $x$ and replace $y$ with $x$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set $y = -3(x - 2)^2 + 14$ and rearrange to isolate $(x - 2)^2$:\n$$3(x - 2)^2 = 14 - y \\implies (x - 2)^2 = \\frac{14 - y}{3}$$",
        "Take the negative square root since the domain is $x \\le 2$ (so $x - 2 \\le 0$):\n$$x - 2 = -\\sqrt{\\frac{14 - y}{3}} \\implies x = 2 - \\sqrt{\\frac{14 - y}{3}}$$",
        "Write the inverse function in terms of $x$:\n$$f^{-1}(x) = 2 - \\sqrt{\\frac{14 - x}{3}}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
